questions.question:
XeF₄ reacts with SbF₅ to form
[XeF_{m}]^{n+} [SbF_{y}]^{z-}
m+n+y+z = _________

questions.explanation:
XeF_{4} + SbF_{5} \to [XeF_{3}]^{+} (SbF_{6})^{-}
m + n + x + y = 3 + 1 + 6 + 1 = 11
Xenon fluoride act as F⁻ donor and F⁻ acceptor.

Positive electron gain enthalpy of inert gases is in order of
\text{Ne} \gt \text{Ar} = \text{Kr} \gt \text{Xe} \gt \text{He}
Comparing this order with the given options, the correct order among the listed elements (He, Xe, Kr, Ne) is \( \text{He} \lt \text{Xe} \lt \text{Kr} \lt \text{Ne} \).
